  {
    "episode_id": 51681,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/5/1/51681.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 32,
    "turn_text": "Oh sure, we had a battalion commander when I was there in Vicenza, Thomas Needham, and his nickname was Newcomb Needham. And I'm telling you, he was tough on officers. As a matter of fact, the first thing that you did as a new officer coming to that battalion in Vicenza, you had to go with a personal run with the battalion commander, Lieutenant Colonel Needham. and you had to climb Mount Barrico. Now it was about from our base to Mount Barrico to the base of it was about three miles and then to go up Mount Barrico and I mean straight up Mount Barrico that was about another mile a mile and a half and then come all the way back. And so, if you didn't keep up with the battalion commander you're gone.",
