  {
    "episode_id": 51681,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/5/1/51681.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 38,
    "turn_text": "Well, without a doubt, you got to be able to soften it a little bit when you're dealing with civilians, but you still have to be the person that maintains and exudes those characteristics and those traits. Your honor, your integrity, your character, I mean, you went to West Point, duty, honor, and country. Those are three very important things. So duty and honor and your integrity, I used to tell young officers, you know, if you don't maintain high standards of integrity, you know, our unit is not the place for you to be in. And I think that that's what you have to continue to do. And that was one of the frustrating things in being a member of Congress is that, you know, we take an oath to support and defend the Constitution. And you would think that elected officials would honor the same thing because supposedly they take an oath to support and defend the Constitution, but they don't. you know, growing up in the military is not about, you know, your self-interest. It's about the interests of your troops. And so you would figure that these, some of these elected officials, instead of self-interest and special interests, that's the problem that we have in our country. And so your honor, integrity and character cannot be taken away from you. It's something that you surrender and sadly, I saw quite a few people watching DC surrender theirs because they just wanted to be part of the in crowd. They wanted to get the campaign donations. They wanted to get the, you know, the lobbyists support. And I remember a funny time when, you know, they asked me to come join them and go down to the Capitol Grill, downtown Washington, D.C., and get a nice big steak dinner. And I told him, hey, you know, when I'm walking home, there's a Popeyes chicken. I'm good to go, man. Because, you know, I live a life of eating MREs and, you know, looking for old water. So I don't need a steak dinner to, to defy who I am. And, and if you do so, then you start to forget whose interest you're there to represent.",
