    "turn_text": "senior, some of these folks are junior, they're off to go get their MBA. There's a lot of different listeners that we have. And one of the conversations I have with a lot of them is I kind of try to help them with transition and stuff. Some of them have thought, hey, maybe getting into politics is something I'm interested in. It's another way to serve. It's another way to continue this DNA that I'm just already programmed with. How would you tell somebody, would you advise that's a good idea? Would you advise that you just be prepared? What are some of the things to think about for anybody looking to go that direction? Because it seems natural, but I imagine we get a lot of, there's a stigma around it. You might lose your souls, would you hear?",
