    "turn_idx": 47,
    "turn_text": "No, absolutely. I do say that we need more, you know, veterans that are running for elected office. I don't care for city council, school board, county commission, you know, state house level all the way up to the federal government level. And that's why back in 2011, we created this organization called the Guardian Fund. If I was going to support a PAC, it was going to be a PAC that sought to get more military and minority conservatives elected to federal office. And, you know, it's been around for 10 years and it's had incredible success. And when I look at a lot of these military members that are running in this cycle and to be able to go out and lend support to them and writing endorsement for them, you know, that's what I want to see happen. And I think that we can restore this constitutional republic to a greatness. If we get people that understand what it means to be willing to lay down your life for something that you believe in, to put the interests of others above your own interests, which is what we learn in the military. So I'm proud to see so many military veterans that are running for office now and also holding different positions. I mean, you look at a guy like Brigadier General Don Bowdoin up in New Hampshire. I",
