    "turn_text": "but we were able to execute because we trained and we understood our tactics, our techniques and our procedures. And that's what you want to be able to do every day as a business leader is always be grounded and rooted in those principles of business that are successful and are time-proven and work. But when you look at Iraq and Afghanistan, it was completely different. Now we're fighting an insurgency. Uh, type of operation, you know, the, the, the enemy is not wearing a uniform. The enemy is blending in with the civilian population. And so you've got to be flexible and have to be able to adjust. And, you know, one of the things we used to say in the military is simple, dumb, be always flexible. But it is so important because the real leader that wins on a battlefield is the one that can adapt and improvise and overcome the quickest. And that's what you have to do. You know, when you sit down, and this is also true, I think, in the business side, if you sit down, you're trying to come up with a 100% plan. You're wasting time. Come up with a good 70 to 75% plan that you can execute to 100% effectiveness. Because as you well know, the enemy always has a",
