    "turn_text": "As Mike Tyson used to say, everyone's got a plan until they get hit in the mouth. Okay, and the failures of combat leaders that I saw were the ones to try to come up with that 100% plan, and they were just totally, you know, wedded to it. And then when the enemy does something different, they're like, which way did he go? What do I do now? And so you've got to come up with those branches and sequels, you know, we're talking about those those courses of action, you have to understand what your opposition could do and the opposition or is the business environment. I mean, think about it. People out there in the business, well, how do you deal with what's going on with supply chain issues? How do you deal with what's going on with fuel issues? How do you deal with what's going on when you can't find enough people to hire? So you always have to think about what is the worst case scenario? And that's what you have to try to plan for. And that's the exact same thing. So it's a huge difference between being that garrison commander, being that combat commander. But it was a huge difference with Desert Shield Desert Storm open mounted desert warfare to what we saw in Iraq and Afghanistan.",
