    "turn_text": "Absolutely. And then I will tell them then. You don't understand is that you're as distant from them as China because they just see you as the person sitting up there in the office and they don't understand any of the reasons why you were doing something. I'll give you a great case in point. You know, when I was a battalion commander in the fourth infantry division, Fort Hood, Texas, and knowing that we're going to be deploying to go over to Iraq, you know, I told our unit that we're going to do some dismounted infantry tactic training. And then we're going to get to go out to the convoy live training lane so that we can learn how to react to ambushes. You should have heard, you know, why we got to do that? You know, some of the old artillery. We're artillery. We don't need to do that. And I say, let me tell you what, What if you get to Iraq, and you're told to park your howitzers, park your, you know, your, your rocket launchers, and you got to mount up and go out and do patrols? And guess",
