    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/5/1/51681.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 77,
    "turn_text": "That's exactly what happened. You know, we got detailed a Bradley linebacker, the ADA company. And our guys had to learn mounted and dismounted infrastructure tactics. And of course, when you get out there on the road, you got the IEDs and everything, you got to learn how to immediately react. And so that's what we did. And guess what? Never lost a guy in a combat engagement because they knew exactly how to respond. So that's what you have to do as a leader. You have to always understand what is the scenario that could come up that maybe we're not expecting right now, but it could happen. because that's how you win on a battlefield. That's how you win in business. No one, I don't think anyone could have ever thought that one day someone's going to sit back and say, my business is not essential. And you got to shut it down. But someone should have sat back and, you know, war gained. Remember how we were there? And said, what's the worst thing that could happen to us as we go into this thing called COVID? less plan for someone tells us we got shut down. What do we do? How do we communicate? How do we continue to be an effective business organization? And so those are the type of things that leaders have to be able to do.",
