    "turn_text": "growth and a lot of companies are focused on that. Often, the person at the helm, the CEO, will be very focused on the growth piece. And I remember in the service being focused on the guys, when things were going, well, I just kind of let my right hand person, you know, always, they allowed the momentum to keep going. And I was always thinking about, well, how would I kill me right now? How would I mess myself up right now? We always thought kind of counter to what was being productive. just to be able to kind of adapt to those things. Is there any advice or recommendations you can give to folks that it's really easy to ride that train when it's going well? How have you kind of been able to stay on the, you know, keep your edge, so to speak?",
