    "turn_idx": 97,
    "turn_text": "Well, I'll be, you know, very honest. There was a little bit of hurt in that you know that your side, your team had betrayed you, kind of stuck you in the back because that doesn't happen in the military. You don't stick your brother's sister in the back in the combat zone. You're going to get someone hurt. And so that was something I had to process through. But the most important thing is my faith in my Lord and Savior, Jesus Christ. And I said, okay, God, you only meant for me to be there for a season. What do you want me to continue to do? And the most important thing is that you continue to be a voice for those principles and values that you believed in. And you continue to press on. So says coming out of Congress, written three books. headed up a Christian ministry center, headed up a conservative policy think tank, you know, been the chairman of the Republican Party of Texas, ran for governor even. and continue to get asked to be on and get my commentary on media. And now I have my own podcast, probably not as good as yours, but I have my own podcast. And so what you have to do is always have that servant mentality in mindset that says it's not about me, it's not about a title, but where can I be to fill the gap? It's kind of like being that reserve unit that someone's holding back and when they see that, hey, you got to get over here because you got to plug that gap that's coming because the bad guys are trying to take our flank or whatever. That's a good position to be in. is to be that necessary tool that this country needs at a critical point in time in this evolution, and to be a voice, you know, for so many men and women in the military that right now, there are a lot of things that they wish they could say, but they can say, but still to this point to get, you know, phone call, email, text, whatever, say, hey, Colonel, These are some of the things that's going on in the military. Can you speak out for us like, for instance, the Coast Guard rescue swimmer who just recently got the phone call from President Biden. But he's looking in 30 to 60 days, getting kicked out of the Coast Guard because he doesn't want to take the COVID shot. And so to be able to be a voice for him and to have his wife contact you and say, please, Colonel, do what you can for us because we love the Coast Guard. We want to continue to serve. To me, that means everything. That's what leadership is about. It's about being a servant, first and",
