    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/5/1/51681.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 104,
    "turn_text": "yeah, that's who is the most important, the newest one, because you got to inculcate him into this culture that we have in that unit. And so it is about doing the little things and that's even out of the Bible and the parable of the of the service where Jesus talked about the ones that were entrusted with much and then the ones that were not entrusted with as much, but the ones that were not entrusted with as much, they still did it with the utmost of their ability. And he said, if you can be trusted and you can accomplish the little things, you're gonna do all the big things, the great things, but if you are not willing to go out there and do some of the big things, maybe you're not the one that's to be entrusted. So I think that again, everything, when you're that leader, you gotta be able to prioritize it, but you gotta understand that one person, and again, it comes back to Jesus, he will leave the 99 to go get the one. So that's where you have to make sure that you have that balance and focus.",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_00",
    "inferred_speaker_name": null,
    "inferred_speaker_role": null,
    "chosen_text_key": "transcript",
